 "about": [
  "Fukuchiyo Shuzo brews Nabeshima in Hamamachi, an old street of clay-walled storehouses in Kashima, Saga, near the Ariake Sea. The brewery was founded in 1923 and marked its centenary in 2023.",
  "Nabeshima, which shares its name with the clan that ruled Saga, was launched in 1998. In 2011 it was named Champion Sake at the International Wine Challenge.",
  "Several of the brewery's buildings, including its koji room and an old rice mill, are registered cultural properties. The mill, about a century old, kept its clay walls when it reopened as a gallery in 2014."
